From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: odin-port <odin@port.local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 22:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: qcom,smbchg: add USB role switch

The qcom-smbchg driver calls usb_role_switch_get() and uses the resulting
switch for USB device/host changes detected by the PMIC. Document the
phandle consumed by that code so boards can connect the charger to their
dual-role controller.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../bindings/power/supply/qcom,smbchg.yaml           | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,smbchg.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,smbchg.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,smbchg.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/qcom,smbchg.yaml
@@ -30,6 +30,12 @@ properties:
       properties must be set.
       See Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/battery.yaml
-
+
+  usb-role-switch:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      Phandle to the USB controller role switch driven from the PMIC USB
+      and USB ID detection state.
+
   interrupts:
     items:
       - description: Charger error
